      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a business prioritizes the bottom line, maximizing output at the cost of human dignity or brand trust often erodes long-term profitability once that reputation takes a hit. The most sustainable \"minimum waste\" strategy is not replacing humans entirely but leveraging AI to augment their capabilities, which actually reduces the cost per unit of value produced without incurring the hidden waste of turnover and legal risk. If you eliminate high performers for a machine that is more expensive to replace or support than the human, you are in fact maximizing cost, not saving it.",
